{
  "task_description": "{'component_name': 'Main Container for CryptoLearn Interactive', 'description': 'Primary container for CryptoLearn Interactive implementation: CryptoPlayground is a client-side web application designed to educate users about cryptographic algorithms through interactive visualizations, hands-on encryption/decryption, and educational content. It simulates Caesar Cipher, AES, and SHA-256, allowing users to experiment with inputs, observe animated algorithm steps, and learn through explanations and quizzes. The app is built with React.js, uses crypto-js for cryptography, Canvas API for animations, Chart.js for performance comparison, and Tailwind CSS for styling. All computations are performed in-browser, with no backend, and the app is accessible and responsive.', 'framework': 'react', 'platform': 'web', 'container': '{\n  "name": "ColorCraft frontend Container",\n  "features": [\n    {\n      "name": "Algorithm Simulations",\n      "description": "Simulate Caesar Cipher, AES (128-bit), and SHA-256. Users can input plaintext and keys, and see animated encryption/decryption or hash computation steps.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Interactive Visualizations",\n      "description": "Canvas-based animations illustrate algorithm steps (e.g., letter shifts, XOR operations). Users can play, pause, rewind, and adjust animation speed.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Try-It-Yourself Editor",\n      "description": "Real-time editor for users to input text and keys, perform encryption/decryption, and view outputs. Input validation ensures correct formats and key lengths.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Educational Content",\n      "description": "Explanations of each algorithm, their mechanics, use cases, and security properties. Includes a mini-quiz per algorithm with results saved in LocalStorage.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Performance Comparison",\n      "description": "Measures and compares execution time of algorithms using JavaScript\\u2019s performance API. Results are displayed in a Chart.js bar chart.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    }\n  ],\n  "techStack": {\n    "frontend": [\n      "React JS"\n    ],\n    "backend": [\n      "None"\n    ],\n    "language": [\n      "JavaScript (ES6+)"\n    ]\n  },\n  "colors": {\n    "primary": "#000000",\n    "secondary": "#F59E42",\n    "accent": "#22D3EE"\n  },\n  "theme": "dark",\n  "layoutDescription": "The UI features a sidebar or top navigation for algorithm selection (Caesar, AES, SHA-256). The main panel displays the visualization canvas, input editor, and output area. Below or beside, educational content and quizzes are shown. A performance comparison chart is accessible via a tab or section. The design is responsive, modern, and accessible, with clear controls for animation and input."\n}'}",
